# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS REPO IS THE PUBLIC SITE. GitHub Pages serves the repo ROOT — the
# files listed below are the ones students load, and everything tracked
# here is world-readable at a stable URL. (`github_pages/` is a local
# mirror that has never been committed; it is not the deploy.)
#
# Allow-list deploy. NOTHING in this folder is published unless it is
# explicitly listed below. So any PDFs, reports, notes, or scratch files
# you keep here stay on your computer — even ones you add later.
#
# To publish a new top-level file/folder, add another "!/name" line.
#
# THIS IS A MULTI-STUDENT APP. It lives in a folder named after one
# student, and that is an accident of history, not a scope. Several
# students use it, more will, and each one accumulates tutor-facing
# material — a ledger, a shortlist, a report, class notes. Section 5 is
# what keeps that material out of the public site NO MATTER WHERE IT IS
# PUT. Read it before adding a file about a student anywhere in this tree.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything at the project root by default
/*

# 2) ...then publish ONLY the web app:
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/index.html
!/progress.html
!/exam.html
!/custom.html
!/review.html
!/README.md
!/shared/
!/Linear_Equations_App/
!/Linear_Functions_App/
!/Nonlinear_Functions_App/
!/Systems_and_Expressions_App_v2/
!/Proportionality_App/
!/Statistical_Reasoning_App/
!/Core_Geometry_App/
!/Analytical_Geometry_App/
!/Data_Analysis_Probability_App/
!/Challenge_App/

# 3) Tutor-side tooling. Tracked so it survives a fresh clone. It is served by
#    Pages like everything else, so it must stay free of passwords and student
#    data: the challenge builder derives a student's roster key from their
#    display name and holds no credentials.
!/build_challenge_set.py
!/CHALLENGE_SETS_RUNBOOK.md

# 4) The test toolchain. The APP has no dependencies and no build step — this is
#    only so `npm install && npm test` works on a fresh clone, which is what the
#    jsdom harness in shared/*.test.js needs. node_modules/ stays ignored by the
#    rule above; the lockfile is deliberately not tracked (dev-only, and this is a
#    public site — there is no point publishing an npm dependency tree).
!/package.json

# OS cruft, even inside published folders
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5) TUTOR-FACING MATERIAL — never tracked, at ANY depth.
#
# Rules 1–4 are an allow-list, and an allow-list only guards the ROOT. Put a
# LEDGER.md inside shared/ or any *_App/ — a folder that is already published —
# and it ships to the public site. That hole was open: `shared/LEDGER.md`,
# `Linear_Equations_App/LEDGER.md` and `Challenge_App/notes.md` were all
# publishable. These patterns close it wherever the file lands.
#
# This matters more as the roster grows. Root rule 6 of the house rules: never
# write an assessment of a student into a file the student can read — and every
# file below is world-readable the moment it is tracked. A ledger says what a
# named minor cannot do yet. A shortlist is a list of what they keep getting
# wrong. Neither belongs at a public URL.
#
# These are DENY rules placed last, so they beat every "!" above. If you ever
# need one of these published, do not delete the pattern — that silently opens
# it for every student. Add a single targeted "!" line and say why.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Per-student ledgers — the tutor's record of what is taught, shaky, and due.
LEDGER.md
*LEDGER.md
*ledger.md

# Challenge shortlists — literally "what this named student keeps missing".
challenge_shortlist_*.md

# Class notes, session plans, and performance reports, wherever they are kept.
Class Summaries/
*Session_Plan*.html
*Performance Report*
*performance_report*

# A general escape hatch: name anything tutor-only with this suffix and it can
# never be published by accident, wherever you put it.
*.tutor.md
*.tutor.json

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY PUBLISHED, and one thing to decide
#
# Tracked here = world-readable. Never allow-list a file holding a password or
# a key.
#
# Note the tutor tooling in rule 3 (build_challenge_set.py,
# CHALLENGE_SETS_RUNBOOK.md) IS published — it is allow-listed above. An earlier
# version of this note claimed it "stays local", and README.md still says the
# same; both were wrong and reassuring in the wrong direction. The tooling holds
# no credentials, but it does carry a student roster key and display name, so it
# names students on the public site.
#
# That is a live decision, not a bug to fix silently: either keep it tracked so
# it survives a fresh clone (today's behaviour) or drop the two "!" lines in
# rule 3 and keep it local. Tutor's call.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
